c7e3c-0d0e-5c12-afc8-020d832fd510" :question/math-academy-id "q-130621" :question/problem "If $K=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -3 & -9\\end{aligned}]$, then ${K}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "Computing ${K}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{2} & =K\\cdot K \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -3 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -3 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, since ${K}^{2}=O,$ the matrix $K$ is a nilpotent matrix of index $2.$ \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${K}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{2} & ={K}^{2}\\cdot {K}^{2} \\\\  & =O\\cdot O \\\\  & =O\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{K}^{4}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cc8dc1a1-9606-5b67-942e-219ab2ddfc1c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of a Nilpotent Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8ddd21a-c8e7-543a-87d1-a12e94066ead" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183668} {:answer/id #uuid "c6548841-aceb-5070-841a-581722797e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183669} {:answer/id #uuid "2ed08120-4bd8-533c-be47-1a6b1c5a1a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183670} {:answer/id #uuid "40380715-6a92-558b-be07-6afe14249b63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183671} {:an